# finfor core agent rules

Treat `/spec` as the source of truth. Index: `spec/README.md`. Specs win over ad-hoc ideas — update the spec first when requirements change.

## Monorepo

| Workspace | Stack |
|-----------|-------|
| `apps/backend` | Node.js 24, Fastify API |
| `apps/frontend` | React 19.2.3, Expo SDK 56 |
| `spec/` | Engineering, UX, product guidelines |

## Mandatory reading by task

| Task | Read |
|------|------|
| Architecture (shared) | `spec/00-shared-architecture-directives.md` |
| Backend | `spec/05-backend-architecture-directives.md` |
| Frontend | `spec/06-frontend-architecture-directives.md` |
| Testing | `spec/07-monorepo-testing-strategy.md` |
| UI / layout / styling | `01` → `02` → `03-page-layout-guidelines.md` → `04-ai-aesthetic-guardrails.md` |
| Product / domain / journeys | `spec/prd.md`, `08`–`18` (update when scope, UI copy, API contracts, or domain rules change) |

## Policies

- Do not break the content-first visual direction in specs `01`–`04`.
- For UI work: state which specs were applied and any deviation.
- If aesthetics conflict with engineering, propose alternatives before a degraded fallback.

## CI (PRs must pass)

Typecheck → unit tests → backend integration → frontend component (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`).
